[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hello, I'm writing on behalf of a team of undergrads from the University of Washington Math AI Lab regarding a project that we hope to PR. We're working on Lean implementations of some linear algebra algorithms. These algorithms compute values with proofs of correctness, which we hope can be used as a teaching tool, as well as making Lean a better language for general-purpose programming. We are planning to PR algorithms for</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Gaussian elimination</li>\n<li>Gauss-Jordan elimination</li>\n<li>LU decomposition (proof incomplete)</li>\n<li>Determinant computation via row reduction (proof incomplete),<br>\nas well as basic definitions and lemmas about row echelon form and reduced row echelon form. We will be ready to PR what we have as soon as we finish proving LU and determinant.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Our hope is for this code to live in <code>mathlib</code>, despite its focus on theory rather over computation. These algorithms are central to standard undergraduate exposition of linear algebra, and would provide a way for people to work with concrete examples. We were wondering what the mathlib community thinks of this approach, and whether this is indeed the right place for this code to live.</p>\n<p>There is one additional question that comes up - if we want this code to be used for general purpose programming, we would like for there to be a fast implementation for matrices to improve the runtimes for our algorithms. Our idea is to use Vectors:<br>\n<code>abbrev FastMatrix (m n : Nat) (R : Type) := Vector (Vector R n) m</code><br>\nWhat would be the best way to approach this? Currently, our code integrates with the existing infrastructure for matrices, but if we create a new \"fast\" data type, should we build out a new library with its own set of facts proved about this data type, or would it be better to simply define the data type and prove that it is equivalent to the existing matrix representation?</p>",
        "id": 584331868,
        "sender_full_name": "Joseph Qian",
        "timestamp": 1775691968
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Great! We definitely need such algorithms.</p>\n<p>I think there should indeed be a <code>FastMatrix</code>, just like there is <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Nat.fastFib#doc\">docs#Nat.fastFib</a>.<br>\nI don't think there should be a lot of theory about it, but rather:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the equivalence with <code>Matrix</code></li>\n<li>fast algorithms</li>\n<li>theorems about those algorithms</li>\n</ul>\n<p>When theory is needed, this should be transported from <code>Matrix</code>. Unfortunately, there is not yet much in terms of good transportation tooling.</p>",
        "id": 584369703,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1775716364
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"678361\">@Yudai Yamazaki</span> has a computable proved version of LU decomposition, as well as echelon form</p>",
        "id": 584714549,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1775838780
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Can I suggest/request the name <code>DenseMatrix</code> rather than <code>FastMatrix</code>?</p>",
        "id": 584787129,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1775870248
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>is there a reason for this? is there a name clash in lean then, or perhaps a \"fast matrix\" is a known concept in literature?</p>",
        "id": 584942654,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1775905641
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'd guess that rather \"dense matrix\" is a known concept in literature.</p>",
        "id": 584942998,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1775905880
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, I'd prefer that the names for computational things are actually about the implementations. E.g. we might also have <code>SparseMatrix</code>, implemented with a <code>TreeMap (Nat x Nat) X</code>, or maybe a band structure + a map.</p>",
        "id": 584948501,
        "sender_full_name": "Kim Morrison",
        "timestamp": 1775910699
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>i see, that makes sense</p>",
        "id": 584948658,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1775910846
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I am working in a <a href=\"https://github.com/miguelmarco/SmithForm\">project</a> with a similar idea in mind, but aiming specifically at the Smith form of matrices over euclidean domains.</p>\n<p>My experience with it is that you actually need to prove more theorems than you expected in the beginning, even if you use the approach of proving equivalence with Mathlib's matrices, and then using it to translate the properties to your structures.</p>",
        "id": 584967870,
        "sender_full_name": "Miguel Marco",
        "timestamp": 1775927806
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hello again,<br>\nWe have decided to proceed with a 1D array representation of matrices and have written two implementations for matrix multiplication.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DenseMatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">data</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Our first approach is simpler and directly modifies a Vector. However, it begins with the call Vector.replicate (m * n) 0, which allocates space for the matrix then initializes it as the 0 vector, resulting in an O(m * n) overhead.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- Approach 1</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Pros: much easier to write proofs about</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Cons: O(m*n) overhead from setting initial values, but this becomes negligible as k → ∞ (since</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- matrix multiplication is O(m * k * n))</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_easy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Add</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Mul</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DenseMatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DenseMatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DenseMatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Id</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Vector</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">replicate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">set!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">data</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The second approach avoids that overhead by working with an Array before casting it to a Vector R (m * n) at the end. This requires a proof that the final Array has size m * n.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- Approach 2</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Pros: Theoretically faster than mul_easy</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Cons: Only makes a difference in practice for small k (up to a max of a factor of 2 when k=1),</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">--       harder to write proofs about</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">dot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DenseMatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">DenseMatrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">dot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">l</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">else</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">sum</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">add_row_size_invariant</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h_size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_helper_size_invariant</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h_size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hi</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">entry</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_helper</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Inhabited</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">out</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Array</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"